  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Plants-4-Hunger: Feed People, Protect the Planet</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations has urged that we will need to produce 70% more food by 2050 without using any more land. According to the UN, we could feed 3.5 billion more people simply by growing crops for human consumption on land currently used to grow feed for livestock. Our Plants-4-Hunger program sponsors plant-based feeding, farming and disaster food relief projects around the world that feed more people using far less land, water, and energy, while protecting animals, ecosystems, and the climate.</narrative>
  </description>
